# A program sets the size of the text area with xterm's CSI 8 ; rows ;
# columns t, while vtium.conf's allow-window-ops is on (vtium/vtium#44).
# vtium meets the request by changing the font size: it draws at the
# largest font size at which the display holds the rows and columns asked
# for, on exactly that grid. The run turns the key on with DEMO_ARGS,
# since it is off by default.
#
#   make vt-check GUIDE=window DEMO_ARGS='--allow-window-ops'

title: a program sets the text area's size

step: A program asks for 80 columns and 25 rows
run: printf '\033[8;25;80t'; sleep 1; echo "rows and columns: $(stty size)"
expect: the text grows to the largest size at which the screen holds 25
expect: rows of 80 columns. The text area is exactly 80 by 25: a band at
expect: the right or at the bottom stays blank where the screen has room
expect: left over. The command prints "rows and columns: 25 80".

step: The size report answers the new size
run: printf '\033[18t'; IFS= read -rs -d t -n 32 -t 2 r; echo "report: ${r#?}t"
expect: the command prints "report: [8;25;80t", the size report's answer of
expect: 25 rows and 80 columns.

step: A zoom fills the screen again
do: press Ctrl and minus once, then Ctrl and plus once.
expect: after Ctrl and minus, the text is smaller and fills the whole
expect: screen, with no blank band. Ctrl and plus makes it larger again,
expect: still filling the screen.
